<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto III, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">980–1002</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto III became King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> at the age of three in 983 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a> in 996. Influenced by his Byzantine mother Theophanu, he dreamed of renewing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-gniezno">Congress of Gniezno</a> in 1000 he honoured Bolesław I and created an archbishopric for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. He died aged 21 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1002.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-iii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Otto III, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="351" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clm_4453_fol_24r_Detail_Herrscherbild.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
